{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013s1WZSfGfXSVZQ4eBj6idY","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tname: invoice-db-url-env-var\n3\tdescription: \"Invoice service must read its DB connection string from INVOICE_DB_URL, never DATABASE_URL\"\n4\tmetadata:\n5\t  node_type: memory\n6\t  type: project\n7\t  originSessionId: 1b942f19-e8d6-45bd-a4a5-7653cd48411c\n8\t  modified: 2026-11-26T09:35:46.743Z\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\tThis service reads its database connection string from `INVOICE_DB_URL`, never from `DATABASE_URL`. The deploy team settled this name.\n12\t\n13\t**Why:** On the deploy host, `DATABASE_URL` points at the platform's shared database. A service that read it would write invoices into that shared database.\n14\t\n15\t**How to apply:** In any code, config, docs, tests, or Docker/deploy files for this service, use `INVOICE_DB_URL` for the connection string. Don't add a `DATABASE_URL` read or fallback, even as a convenience default. Flag any existing code that does.\n16\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bf7b25c4-53a9-46fe-b9d0-de4d8636cabc","uuid":"4511c83a-9d24-44d2-acb5-8aa888c5d04d","timestamp":"2026-11-26T09:35:54.235Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/johnmarkenriquez/.claude-personal/projects/-private-var-folders-wg-kshmq8sn7zl5m1ch85m7yvvh0000gn-T-invoice-service-bM4LRH/memory/invoice-db-url-env-var.md","content":"---\nname: invoice-db-url-env-var\ndescription: \"Invoice service must read its DB connection string from INVOICE_DB_URL, never DATABASE_URL\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 1b942f19-e8d6-45bd-a4a5-7653cd48411c\n  modified: 2026-11-26T09:35:46.743Z\n---\n\nThis service reads its database connection string from `INVOICE_DB_URL`, never from `DATABASE_URL`. The deploy team settled this name.\n\n**Why:** On the deploy host, `DATABASE_URL` points at the platform's shared database. A service that read it would write invoices into that shared database.\n\n**How to apply:** In any code, config, docs, tests, or Docker/deploy files for this service, use `INVOICE_DB_URL` for the connection string. Don't add a `DATABASE_URL` read or fallback, even as a convenience default. Flag any existing code that does.\n","numLines":16,"startLine":1,"totalLines":16}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_013s1WZSfGfXSVZQ4eBj6idY","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"other"}}]}
